<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Reproduction report · {{ title }}</title>
<style>
:root{--ink:#172e47;--muted:#526477;--line:#cbd6e4;--blue:#245db5;--wash:#eff4fb;--green:#126149;--amber:#8a5412;--white:#fff}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;color:var(--ink);background:white;font:17px/1.65 Aptos,"Segoe UI",Arial,sans-serif}a{color:var(--blue);text-underline-offset:3px}button,input,select{font:inherit}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue);outline-offset:3px}header,main,footer{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:36px 30px}header{padding-top:52px}header .title{font-size:20px;max-width:70ch;margin:14px 0}h1{font-size:clamp(29px,4vw,44px);font-weight:650;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:14px 0}h2{font-size:28px;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 18px}h3{font-size:21px;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 12px}h4{font-size:17px;margin:18px 0 8px}p{max-width:75ch;margin:10px 0 16px}.muted,small{color:var(--muted)}small{font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}.brand{font-weight:600;color:var(--blue)}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 28px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px 0;margin-top:28px}nav a{text-decoration:none;font-size:16px}main{padding-top:0}section{padding:30px 0 42px;scroll-margin-top:20px}section+section{border-top:2px solid var(--line)}.lead{font-size:20px;line-height:1.5}.notice{padding:18px 22px;background:var(--wash);border-left:5px solid var(--blue);margin:22px 0}.notice.warning{border-color:var(--amber)}.notice p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px;margin:26px 0}.facts>div{border-top:4px solid var(--blue);padding-top:14px}.facts b{font-size:21px;display:block}.facts p{font-size:16px;margin:5px 0}.issue{margin:26px 0 38px}.issue>p{max-width:72ch}.cause{padding-left:18px;border-left:3px solid var(--line)}details{border:1px solid var(--line);margin:14px 0;background:white}summary{cursor:pointer;padding:13px 16px;font-weight:600;font-size:16px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}details>.inner{padding:0 18px 18px}details details{border-inline:0}blockquote{font:17px/1.6 Georgia,serif;border-left:3px solid var(--blue);padding:10px 18px;margin:14px 0;background:var(--wash);max-width:76ch}.scroll{overflow:auto;max-width:100%}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{background:var(--wash);font-weight:600}td p{margin:0 0 8px}td.n{white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.quantity-label{min-width:210px;max-width:420px}.quantity-label small{display:block;margin-top:6px}.badge{color:var(--green);font-weight:600}.badge.problem{color:var(--amber)}.toolbar{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}.toolbar input{flex:1;min-width:170px}.toolbar input,.toolbar select,select,button{border:1px solid #8498b2;background:white;padding:9px 12px;border-radius:3px;color:var(--ink);max-width:100%}.toolbar select{max-width:300px}.plot{margin:18px 0 8px;width:100%;overflow:auto}.plot-scroll-hint{display:none}.spec-column{cursor:pointer}.spec-column:focus .estimate-point,.spec-column.selected .estimate-point{stroke:#172e47;stroke-width:2}.plot svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.spec-detail{background:var(--wash);padding:20px;margin:16px 0 28px}.spec-detail dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:8px 28px;margin:16px 0}.spec-detail dt{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.spec-detail dd{margin:0;font-size:16px}.selection{display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.selection strong{font-size:19px}.verification td{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.checks-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.check-finding{border-top:3px solid var(--line);padding-top:16px}.check-finding+.check-finding{margin-top:28px}.check-finding p{font-size:16px}.evidence-list{padding-left:22px}.evidence-list li{margin-bottom:10px}code{font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}pre{font-size:13px;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.footnote{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}button{cursor:pointer}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}[hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:650px){.plot-scroll-hint{display:block}header,main,footer{padding-inline:18px}header{padding-top:30px}.facts,.checks-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}.facts>div{border-top-width:2px}.facts b{font-size:19px}.facts p{font-size:16px}section{padding:24px 0 30px}h2{font-size:25px}.spec-detail{padding:16px}.spec-detail dl{grid-template-columns:1fr}.quantity-label{min-width:180px}th,td{padding:10px}nav{gap:8px 18px}.lead{font-size:18px}blockquote{font-size:16px}.notice{padding:15px}summary{padding:12px}}@media print{nav,.toolbar,button{display:none}header,main{max-width:none;padding:12px}body{font-size:11pt}.scroll{overflow:visible}.plot{break-inside:avoid}section{break-before:auto}}
</style></head><body>
{% macro comparison(quantities, compact=false) %}
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Reported quantity</th><th>Paper</th><th>Recalculation</th><th>What the comparison establishes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for q in quantities %}<tr><td class="quantity-label"><a href="#quantity-{{ q.claim_id }}">{{ q.label }}</a><small>{{ q.kind|label }}{% if q.study %} · {{ q.study|label }}{% endif %} · PDF page {{ q.page or 'not recorded' }}</small></td><td class="n">{{ q.comparator }} {{ q.reported|number }}</td><td>{% for r in q.replicas %}<p>{{ r.replicated|number }} <small>({{ r.replica_id|label }})</small></p>{% else %}{{ q.descriptive.value|number if q.descriptive else 'Not computed' }}{% endfor %}</td><td>{{ q.status|capitalize }}{% if not q.replicas and not q.descriptive %}<p><small>{{ q.reason or 'No verified calculation is available.' }}</small></p>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endmacro %}
<header><span class="brand">reproscope</span><h1>Reproduction and sensitivity analysis</h1><p class="title">{{ title }}</p>{% if doi_url %}<a href="{{ doi_url }}">Read the paper</a>{% endif %}
<nav aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#overview">Main findings</a><a href="#divergences">Discrepancy evidence</a><a href="#review">Statistical checks</a><a href="#multiverse">Multiverse</a><a href="#coverage">All reported numbers</a><a href="#audit">Verification</a></nav></header>
<main>
<section id="overview"><h2>What this run establishes</h2>
{% if focal.text %}<p class="lead"><b>The paper’s focal claim:</b> {{ focal.text }}</p>{% endif %}
{% for stage,record in pipeline_status.get('stages',{}).items() %}{% if record.status=='failed' %}<div class="notice warning"><strong>Run incomplete.</strong> {{ {'0':'Source extraction and data binding','1':'Reproduction','2':'Statistical review','3':'Multiverse','report':'Report generation'}.get(stage,stage) }} did not pass: {{ record.error or 'no failure detail recorded' }}. Available evidence is shown below.</div>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
<div class="facts"><div><b>{{ findings.coverage.get('counts',{}).get('computed',0) }} reported quantities computed</b><p>{{ findings.coverage.get('counts',{}).get('unavailable',0) }} lack sufficient inputs; {{ findings.coverage.get('counts',{}).get('invalid_input',0) }} have invalid inputs. {{ findings.coverage.get('counts',{}).get('unresolved',0) }} await a computation disposition.</p></div><div><b>{{ findings.counts.get('check difference',0) }} comparisons need attention</b><p>{{ findings.counts.get('close agreement',0) + findings.counts.get('close descriptive agreement',0) }} closely agree. {{ findings.counts.get('close agreement under declared convention',0) }} agree under a reconstruction convention.</p></div><div><b>{% if reader.fully_verified %}{{ reader.reference.checked }} multiverse specifications verified{% else %}Multiverse verification incomplete{% endif %}</b><p>{% if s3 and not s3.abstained %}{{ findings.sensitivity.active_dimensions|length }} analytical dimensions; {{ findings.sensitivity.groups|length }} separately labelled effect groups.{% else %}No current accepted sensitivity result.{% endif %}</p></div></div>
{% if focal.replica_values %}<div class="notice"><p><b>Focal {{ focal.quantity_kind|label }}:</b> the paper reports {{ focal.claim.value|number if focal.claim else focal.reported.value|number }}. {% for r in focal.replica_values %}{{ r.replica_id|label }} gives {{ r.value }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% else %}.{% endif %}{% endfor %} <a href="#quantity-{{ focal.claim_id }}">Inspect its source and method evidence</a>.</p>{% for q in findings.quantities if q.claim_id==focal.claim_id %}<p><b>Comparison:</b> {{ q.status|capitalize }}.{% set direction=namespace(consistent=q.replicas|length>0) %}{% for r in q.replicas %}{% if "substantive direction: consistent with source" not in (r.rule or "") %}{% set direction.consistent=false %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if direction.consistent %} The paired calculations agree in magnitude and substantive direction. Opposite subtraction orders can produce opposite signs; the paper does not specify its subtraction order.{% endif %}</p>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
<p>Counts refer to source quantities, not independent tests. A reproduced number establishes a route from the deposited data to that result. A discrepancy alone does not establish an error in the original analysis.</p>
{% if reader.topics %}<p><b>Issues to inspect:</b> {% for t in reader.topics[:3] %}<a href="#issue-{{ loop.index }}">{{ t.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}; {% else %}.{% endif %}{% endfor %} <a href="#divergences">See all {{ reader.topics|length }} issue topics</a>.</p>{% endif %}
</section>
<section id="divergences"><h2>Discrepancies and their causes</h2>{% if not s1 %}<p>Stage 1 not run.</p>{% endif %}<p>Each issue links the reported number to its recalculation and source. Unavailable inputs and unresolved analysis choices remain explicit.</p>
{% for t in reader.topics %}<article class="issue" id="issue-{{ loop.index }}"><h3>{{ t.title }}</h3><p>{{ t.finding }}</p>{% if t.cause %}<p class="cause"><b>Cause:</b> {{ t.cause }}</p>{% endif %}<p><b>What would resolve it:</b> {{ t.next_check }}</p>
<small>{% for status,n in t.evidence_status.items() %}{{ n }} {{ status|label }} diagnosis group{{ 's' if n!=1 else '' }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}. {{ t.quantities|length }} source quantities covered.</small>
{{ comparison(t.quantities[:4],true) }}{% if t.quantities|length>4 %}<details><summary>{{ t.quantities|length-4 }} more affected quantities</summary><div class="inner">{{ comparison(t.quantities[4:],true) }}</div></details>{% endif %}
<details><summary>Source evidence and detailed diagnosis</summary><div class="inner">{% for d in t.diagnoses %}<h4>{{ d.evidence_status|label|capitalize }}</h4><p>{{ d.explanation }}</p>{% set quote = d.evidence_quote|prose_evidence %}{% if quote and quote != d.explanation %}<blockquote>{{ quote }}</blockquote>{% endif %}<small>See the linked source quantities above for the paper text and calculation inputs.</small>{% endfor %}</div></details></article>{% else %}<p>No completed divergence diagnosis is available. This does not establish that all quantities agree.</p>{% endfor %}
</section>
<section id="review"><h2>Statistical analysis and interpretation</h2><p>The checks ask whether the available evidence establishes a clear statistical error or a clear interpretation error. Replica code is not author code.</p>
{% if s2 and s2.questions %}{% for key,title in [('coding','Statistical analysis'),('interpretation','Interpretation')] %}{% set q=s2.questions.get(key,{}) %}<h3>{{ title }}</h3><p>{{ q.get('summary','No completed assessment.') }}</p>{% for f in q.get('findings',[]) %}<article class="check-finding"><h4>{{ f.error }}</h4><p><b>Evidence status:</b> {{ f.evidence_status|label }}.</p><p>{{ f.consequence }}</p>{% for link in f.issue_links %}<p><a href="#issue-{{ link.index }}">Discrepancy evidence: {{ link.title }}</a></p>{% endfor %}<details><summary>Reasoning, source and next check</summary><div class="inner"><p>{{ f.demonstration }}</p><p><b>Next check:</b> {{ f.next_check }}</p>{% set anchor = f.anchor|prose_evidence %}{% if anchor %}<blockquote>{{ anchor }}</blockquote>{% endif %}{% for q in f.quantity_links %}<a href="#quantity-{{ q.claim_id }}">{{ q.kind|label }} = {{ q.value|number }}{% if q.page %} (PDF p. {{ q.page }}){% endif %}</a>{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div></details></article>{% endfor %}{% if q.get('limitations') %}<details><summary>Limits of this assessment</summary><div class="inner">{% for l in q.limitations %}<p>{{ l }}</p>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% elif s2 %}<p>This archive contains a review from an earlier reporting protocol.</p><div>{{ s2.review_html }}</div>{% else %}<p>Stage 2 not run. No completed statistical review is available.</p>{% endif %}
<p class="footnote">No clear error found means none was established within the inspected evidence; it does not prove that the analysis is error-free.</p></section>
<section id="multiverse"><h2>How analytical choices affect the result</h2>
{% if not s3 %}<p>Stage 3 not run.</p>{% elif s3.abstained %}<div class="notice warning"><p>{{ s3.abstain_reason }}</p><p>Attempted outputs do not constitute an accepted multiverse.</p></div>{% else %}
<p>The curve and choice panels follow the <a href="https://masurp.github.io/specr/reference/plot.specr.object.html">specr format</a>. {{ findings.sensitivity.n_analytical }} analytical specifications were run across {{ findings.sensitivity.active_dimensions|length }} varying dimensions.{% if s3.sampled %} They form a stratified sample of {{ s3.grid_size }} compatible combinations ({{ (100*s3.sample_fraction)|number }}% coverage). Conclusions apply to the executed sample.{% else %} These cover the full compatible grid.{% endif %} {{ findings.sensitivity.failures|length }} specifications failed.</p>
{% if reader.fully_verified %}<p class="badge">Every executed specification passed independent numerical checks on the deposited data and on a private resampled copy.</p>{% else %}<div class="notice warning">Independent verification is incomplete. These outputs cannot support a completed-run claim.</div>{% endif %}
{% if s3.interpretation_html %}<div class="multiverse-reading">{{ s3.interpretation_html }}</div>{% endif %}
<p>Each curve contains comparable effect estimates; tests of different null hypotheses are summarised separately. Each column is one analytical specification, including choices that change only inference. Specifications share data and are not independent votes.</p>
{% if reader.assumptions %}<details><summary>Assumptions and limits of these alternatives</summary><div class="inner">{% for a in reader.assumptions %}<p>{{ a }}</p>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% endif %}
{% for g in findings.sensitivity.groups %}<article class="effect-group" data-group="{{ loop.index0 }}"><h3>{{ g.label }}</h3><p><b>{{ g.min|number }} to {{ g.max|number }}</b> across {{ g.n }} specifications (median {{ g.median|number }}). {{ g.intervals }} have confidence intervals. {{ g.positive }} estimates are above and {{ g.negative }} below the null value {{ g.null_value|number }}.</p>
{% set ref=g.reported_reference %}{% if ref.available %}<p class="reported-position"><b>The paper reports {{ ref.value|number }}.</b> {{ ref.below }} specifications {% if ref.precision is not none %}fall below its rounding range{% else %}have lower estimates{% endif %}, {{ ref.tied }} {% if ref.precision is not none %}round to that value at {{ ref.precision }} decimal places{% else %}equal that value{% endif %}, and {{ ref.above }} {% if ref.precision is not none %}fall above that range{% else %}have higher estimates{% endif %}.{% if ref.tied %} The matching specifications occupy ranks {{ ref.rank_low }}{% if ref.rank_high!=ref.rank_low %}–{{ ref.rank_high }}{% endif %} of {{ ref.n }}.{% endif %} <a href="#quantity-{{ ref.claim_id }}">Source</a>. The dashed line marks the reported value{% if ref.precision is not none %}; shading shows its rounding range{% endif %}, not a recovered author specification.</p>{% else %}<p class="footnote reported-position">{{ ref.note }}{% if focal.quantity_kind %} The focal paper value is {{ focal.quantity_kind|label }} = {{ focal.claim.value|number if focal.claim else focal.reported.value|number }}; it is not converted to this curve’s scale.{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
<p class="footnote plot-scroll-hint">Scroll the figure horizontally to see all specifications; the estimates and choices move together.</p><div class="plot" id="plot-{{ loop.index0 }}" aria-label="Specification estimates and aligned analytical choices" tabindex="0">{{ g.svg }}</div><p class="footnote">Both panels share the same specification order. Blue/red marks indicate positive/negative estimates meeting the declared p-value criterion; grey marks do not. Confidence intervals need not encode that criterion. Select a column to inspect its calculation. On narrow screens, scroll both panels together.</p><button type="button" id="download-{{ loop.index0 }}">Download interactive figure (SVG)</button>{% if g.specr_download %} <a href="{{ g.specr_download }}" download="specr-{{ loop.index }}.svg">Download R/specr figure</a>{% endif %}
<div class="spec-detail" id="detail-{{ loop.index0 }}"><div class="selection"><label for="select-{{ loop.index0 }}">Inspect specification</label><select id="select-{{ loop.index0 }}">{% for r in g.rows %}<option value="{{ loop.index0 }}">{{ r.spec_id or loop.index }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div><div class="spec-content"></div></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Tested null</th><th>p used for comparison</th><th>Below the declared threshold</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for n in g.inference %}<tr><td>{{ n.label }}</td><td>{{ n.p_min|number }} to {{ n.p_max|number }}</td><td>{{ n.significant }} / {{ n.n_p }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<details><summary>Which decisions change the result?</summary><div class="inner"><p>Matched comparisons hold all other settings fixed. Missing comparisons mean that the executed grid does not identify that change. A zero estimate change can accompany different uncertainty.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Matched sets</th><th>Largest estimate change</th><th>Largest p change within one null</th><th>Largest interval-width change</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for c in g.changes %}<tr><td>{{ c.label }}</td><td>{{ c.matched_sets }}</td><td>{{ c.max_change|number }}</td><td>{{ c.max_p_change|number }}</td><td>{{ c.max_interval_width_change|number }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div></div></details></article>{% endfor %}
{% if findings.sensitivity.diagnostics %}<p>{{ findings.sensitivity.diagnostics|length }} leave-one-out checks are influence diagnostics. They are excluded from analytical dimensions and effect-curve denominators.</p>{% else %}<p class="footnote">Leave-one-out checks are influence diagnostics, not analytical choices; none are counted in this multiverse.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if s3 %}<details><summary>Screening audit: accepted and rejected choices</summary><div class="inner">{% for f in reader.factors %}<h3>{{ f.label }}</h3>{% for l in f.levels %}<h4>{{ l.label }}</h4><p>{{ l.rationale or l.how }}</p><small>{{ l.verdict|label }}{% if l.role %} · {{ l.role|label }}{% endif %}</small>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% for u in s3.unimplementable %}<p><b>{{ u.name|label }}:</b> {{ u.reason }}</p>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% endif %}</section>
<section id="coverage"><h2>Every reported number</h2>
{% if not s0 %}<p>Stage 0 not run.</p>{% else %}<p>{{ findings.quantities|length }} source result records are accounted for. {{ findings.n_metadata }} linked test metadata fields, including degrees of freedom, are checked separately with their test.</p>
{% if s0.extraction_benchmark %}<p><b>Extraction benchmark:</b> {{ s0.extraction_benchmark.accepted_correct }} of {{ s0.extraction_benchmark.clean_source_occurrences }} clean source occurrences recovered ({{ (100*s0.extraction_benchmark.accepted_recall)|number }}% recall; {{ (100*s0.extraction_benchmark.accepted_precision)|number }}% precision).</p><p class="footnote">{{ s0.extraction_benchmark.scope }} Extractor agreement alone is not a correctness score.</p>{% endif %}
<div class="toolbar"><input id="quantity-search" aria-label="Search reported quantities" placeholder="Search an outcome, quote or result ID"><select id="quantity-status" aria-label="Filter quantity status"><option value="">All findings</option>{% for status in findings.counts %}<option value="{{ status }}">{{ status|capitalize }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div><p id="quantity-count" class="footnote" aria-live="polite">{{ findings.quantities|length }} quantities</p>
<div id="quantities">{% for q in findings.quantities %}<details class="quantity-record" id="quantity-{{ q.claim_id }}" data-status="{{ q.status }}"><summary>{{ q.kind|label }} {{ q.comparator }} {{ q.reported|number }} · {{ q.label }} <small>({{ q.claim_id }})</small></summary><div class="inner"><p><b>{{ q.status|capitalize }}</b> · PDF page {{ q.page or 'not recorded' }}{% if q.study %} · {{ q.study|label }}{% endif %}</p><blockquote>{{ q.source or 'No source quote recorded.' }}</blockquote>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Calculation</th><th>Value</th><th>Difference from paper</th><th>Comparison rule</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for r in q.replicas %}<tr><td>{{ r.replica_id|label }}</td><td>{{ r.replicated|number }}</td><td>{{ r.difference|number }}<small>{{ r.difference_basis }}</small></td><td>{{ r.rule or r.comparison_basis or r.outcome_status }}{% if r.sign_convention_status %}<p>{{ r.sign_convention_status }}</p>{% endif %}{% if r.degrees_of_freedom %}<p>Degrees of freedom: {{ r.degrees_of_freedom.status|label }}. {% if r.degrees_of_freedom.status in ['match','mismatch'] %}Reported {{ r.degrees_of_freedom.reported_df }}, computed {{ r.degrees_of_freedom.computed_df }}. {% endif %}{{ r.degrees_of_freedom.reason }}</p>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td>Descriptive calculation</td><td>{{ q.descriptive.value|number if q.descriptive else 'Not computed' }}</td><td>—</td><td>{{ q.descriptive.verification if q.descriptive else q.reason }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
{% if q.reason %}<p>{{ q.reason }}</p>{% endif %}{% if q.binding_scope.get('basis')=='conventional_reconstruction' %}<div class="notice warning"><b>Reconstruction assumption:</b> {{ q.binding_scope.assumptions|join('; ') }}. The comparison cannot distinguish this convention from the original authors’ method.</div>{% endif %}
{% if q.data_bindings %}<h4>Data and model inputs</h4><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Deposited file</th><th>Columns</th><th>Operation</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for b in q.data_bindings %}<tr><td>{{ b.field }}</td><td>{{ b.file }}{% if b.table %}, {{ b.table }}{% endif %}</td><td>{{ b.columns|join(", ") }}</td><td>{{ b.operation }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>{% endif %}
{% if q.readout_evidence is defined %}{% set b=q.readout_evidence %}{% if b.state=="supported" and b.operation %}<p><b>Descriptive method:</b> {{ b.operation }} of {{ b.columns|join(", ") }} in {{ b.file }}{% if b.n %}, using {{ b.n }} observations{% endif %}. {% for f in b.filters %}Filter: {{ f.column }} {{ f.operator }} {{ f.value }}. {% endfor %}{{ b.reason }}</p>{% endif %}{% endif %}
{% for e in q.method_evidence %}<p><b>Independent method check ({{ e.replica_id|label }}):</b> {{ e.status }}; {{ e.family|label }}{% if e.n %}, n = {{ e.n }}{% endif %}{% if e.df %}, df = {{ e.df }}{% endif %}.{% if e.x %} Inputs: {{ e.x }}{% if e.y %} and {{ e.y }}{% endif %}.{% endif %} {{ e.method_scope }}</p>{% endfor %}
{% for alias in q.source_aliases %}<p><b>Source mapping:</b> {{ alias.source_text }} → {{ alias.canonical }}. {{ alias.note }}</p>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}</section>
<section id="audit"><h2>What was verified</h2><p>The executor’s ability to rerun its own code and independent numerical verification are separate checks. Passing one does not substitute for the other.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% if s1 %}{% for r in s1.replicas %}<tr><td>Original-analysis replica: {{ r.replica_id|label }}</td><td>{{ r.script_execution }}; audit {{ r.audit_acceptance }}{% if r.source_repair_models %}<p><small>Generated by {{ r.model }}; targeted source repairs by {{ r.source_repair_models|join(", ") }}.</small></p>{% endif %}</td><td>{% for status,n in r.method_counts.items() %}{{ n }} methods {{ status }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}{% endif %}<tr><td>Multiverse numerical checks</td><td>{{ reader.reference.get('checked',0) }} / {{ reader.reference.get('total','not recorded') }} specifications fully checked; {{ reader.reference.get('status','not established') }}</td><td>{{ reader.verification_scope }}</td></tr><tr><td>Multiverse with resampled input records</td><td>{{ reader.perturbation.get('checked',0) }} / {{ reader.perturbation.get('total','not recorded') }}; {{ reader.perturbation.get('status','not established') }}</td><td>Changes observations while preserving within-person item, total and category relationships; reruns both implementations. An exact untied signed-rank method uses a subset without replacement so the check does not manufacture invalid ties.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>{% if s0 and s0.leak_verdict=="none" %}The packet audit detected no result leakage.{% elif s0 and s0.leak_verdict %}The packet audit identified structural clues: requested statistic fields can suggest which results the paper emphasised. Numerical targets remain withheld, but blinding is limited.{% else %}Packet blinding has not been established.{% endif %}</p>
<p>Independent method recipes use screened methods, blinded contracts and column names. They do not use executor code, plans, computed values or reported targets. A separate model reviews those recipes before numerical checking. This tests the implementation of the stated analysis; it does not establish its substantive assumptions.</p>
<p>Seeded resampling uses a declared generator and draw order. Exact computational agreement is not certainty about a tail probability: finite permutation draws still limit p-value resolution. A fixed source significance threshold can be rescaled for display without inventing a family of uncomputed tests.</p>
<details><summary>Models, cost and run record</summary><div class="inner"><p>Recorded API cost{% if cost_unknown %} allowance{% endif %}: ${{ '%.4f'|format(cost_api) }}.{% if cost_unknown %} Includes ${{ '%.4f'|format(cost_unknown) }} reserved for interrupted calls with unknown charges.{% endif %} Subscription calls are not metered spending.</p><p>{{ ledger.models|join(', ') }}</p><p>Run: <code>{{ paper_id }}</code>. Report generated {{ run_date }}.</p>{% if protocol_provenance %}<p>{{ protocol_provenance.scope }}</p>{% endif %}</div></details>
{% if public_export %}<p class="footnote">This public report includes numerical and source evidence. Participant records, execution logs and local file paths remain in the local archive.</p>{% else %}<details><summary>Local evidence and generated code</summary><div class="inner">{% for a in attachments %}<p><a href="../{{ a.path }}">{{ a.path }}</a></p>{% endfor %}</div></details>{% endif %}</section>
</main><footer>Automated analysis of the available paper and deposit. Unresolved evidence remains unresolved.</footer>
<script id="multiverse-data" type="application/json">{{ findings.sensitivity.groups|tojson }}</script>
{% include 'reader.js.j2' %}
</body></html>
